### Output Format
Respond with XML inside a `<synthesis>` root element (no other text):

```xml
<synthesis pass1_claim_count="{n}" final_claim_count="{n}" merges="{n}" discoveries="{n}">
  <claims>
    <claim id="C1" agreement="consensus" corroboration_count="7" pass1_ref="C1">
      <text>Synthesised claim text</text>
      <sources>
        <source expert_id="expert_01">
          <quote>verbatim quote supporting this claim</quote>
        </source>
      </sources>
      <counterarguments>
        <counterargument>Challenge or rebuttal from R2 deliberation</counterargument>
      </counterarguments>
    </claim>
    <claim id="C5" agreement="divided" corroboration_count="3" pass1_ref="C5,C8" merge_reason="Same mechanism (surveillance risk) from different framing">
      <text>Merged claim text</text>
      <sources>...</sources>
      <counterarguments>...</counterarguments>
    </claim>
  </claims>
  <claim_accounting>
    <merged>
      <merge target="C5" from="C5,C8" reason="Same mechanism from different framing"/>
    </merged>
    <discovered>
      <discovery id="C22" reason="Position found in R2 rebuttal not captured by Pass 1"/>
    </discovered>
  </claim_accounting>
  <areas_of_agreement>
    <area>Area 1</area>
  </areas_of_agreement>
  <areas_of_disagreement>
    <area>Tension 1</area>
  </areas_of_disagreement>
  <uncertainties>
    <uncertainty>Uncertainty 1</uncertainty>
  </uncertainties>
  <minority_reports>
    <report expert_id="expert_03" support_count="1">
      <position>Distinctive minority position</position>
      <evidence><quote>supporting quote</quote></evidence>
      <committee_assessment>Why this wasn't adopted by majority</committee_assessment>
    </report>
  </minority_reports>
  <narrative>Complete narrative with [C1] inline citations [C2, C3].</narrative>
</synthesis>
```

### Emergence space (§6)
If you notice structural patterns, implicit assumptions shared across experts, or tensions between the claim inventory and the deliberation record, surface them in an `<emergence>` element after the narrative.

### Self-check before outputting
1. Count your final claims + documented merges. Does it account for every Pass 1 claim?
2. Are counterarguments populated for every divided/minority claim?
3. Does every substantive narrative sentence have a citation?
